#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|page=422|passage=Josie Powell that was, prettiest '''deb''' in Dublin. How time flies by!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Michael Pakenham|title=The Bitter Web|location=Lewes, Sussex|publisher=The Book Guild Ltd|year=1989|page=41|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bitterweb0000pake/page/41/mode/1up|isbn=0-863-32398-7|passage=Go back to your '''debs''' or little boys if that's what you fancy and leave us hard working girls, the virile, mature and experienced working men of this world.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Harriet Evans|title=Beloved Girls|location=London|publisher=w:Headline Review|year=2021|page=253|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/belovedgirls0000harr/page/253/mode/1up|isbn=978-1-472-25105-3|passage='The Honourable Hester Bingham,' she told Simon. 'They said she was the most stylish '''deb''' of her season. Me and Mama read all about her. That was the first season after the war, you know, and she wote a Hardy Amies dress when she was presented to the King and Queen.'}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Shelley Burr|title=Wake|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:William Morrow|year=2022|page=269|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/wakenovel0000burr/page/269/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-063-23522-9|passage="After that little crash and burn, I guess my mother thought it would help to give me the same training. Social graces and deportment and all that bullshit. I even had a '''deb''' ball."}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A debutante ball or [[debut#Noun|debut]].
#: {{syn|en|debs<qq:informal>}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Gian Sardar|title=You Were Here|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:G. P. Putnam's Sons|year=2017|page=143|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/youwerehere0000sard/page/143/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-399-57500-6|passage="When I met him at my '''deb''', I fell for him. Wanted nothing more than to marry him. That it happened, even after all those years, felt as if the stars had finally aligned."}}
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} A [[female#Adjective|female]] member of a [[gang#Noun|gang]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Hal Ellson|title=Tomboy|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Charles Scribner's Sons|year=1950|page=157|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/tomboy0000hale/page/157/mode/1up|passage=Then one night Liz showed up at the factory with a scratched face and torn blouse. She had been in a fight at the park with another girl, a '''deb''' of the Porto Rican Flyers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Donald Goines|title=Black Gangster|location=Los Angeles, C.A.|publisher=[[w:Kensington Publishing|Holloway House Publishing Company]]|year=1972|year_published=2004<!--per archive.org-->|page=38|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/blackgangster00goin/page/38/mode/1up|isbn=0-870-67992-9|passage=I want you to take over absolute control of all the '''debs''' until Ruby is released. Your main job will be to see that most of the girls take at least two tricks a night someplace where the boys can roll them without too much trouble.}}

